{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987292-questions-about-shapechanging","id":987292,"title":"Questions about Shapechanging","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-14T09:13:58-07:00","id":987292,"title":"Questions about Shapechanging","content":"My questions are specifically related to Mokole. Other questions are welcome in this thread though. Also I realize that some might not have RAW answers, so giving interpretations is fine.<br /> <br /> When a Mokole changes between Suchid and Homid, does their biological thermoregulation change? Do they go from endothermic to exothermic and back? <br /> <br /> A saltwater crocodile can go for months without eating, does this mean their Homid form can as well if they're suchid breed? I'd immediately assume not and that their metabolism depend on their form. Same with their thermoregulation.<br /> <br /> Which leads to my next question: If a Mokole has been in Suchid form for days or weeks without eating and switch to Homid form, are they immediately hungry or will they go from a neutral state to a hungry state at normal Homid pace? Or if they're hungry in Homid form and go to Suchid form will their hunger stop mattering since the Suchid body doesn't need to eat as frequently?<br /> <br /> Can a shapechanger only become pregnant in their breed form? How does the fetus or eggs interact with changing shape? Will they become unable to change shape? More information about this stuff would be nice.<br /> <br /> That's all I could think of off the top of my head, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T11:41:17-07:00","id":987351,"title":"","content":"Thermoregulation: I would say they switch back and forth depending on form. This is based on the merit &quot;temperature control&quot; from the breed book. It states with this merit a Mokol\u00e9 can with concentration control thier body temperature based on need, combinedo with the archives trait back sail (can't remember the exact name) that grants this merit in archive form. Toss in that in such I'd they are meant to be indistinguishable from a normal kin species (a 98.6 degrees croc on a 60 degree day would be distinguished). So those are my thoughts, plus the breed book does say Mokol\u00e9 need less territory due to reptiles needing less food. Lastly Mokol\u00e9 put anew emphasis on basking in the sun. They bring up how the sun is the one who warms thier bodies, they don't bask really in luna'so light. Sure they follow her, but theterrible seems a lack of emphasis on basking in moon light. Toss in the Corax only follow Helios but don't refer to him as the one who warms thier bodies....for me that's another indication of having exothermic tendencies.<br /> <br /> Metabolism: honestly when in such I'd use how long a such I'd can go without food and then be approximate for when they shift homid. So a sated croc becomes a sated homid and a hungry croc becomes a hungry homid.....also go a few months without eating only to shift homid and die seems like overkill, especially since this isn't really covered in the books. Mokol\u00e9 digestion is odd (large Archie's can eat garou, what happens when they shift?) I'd also say a homid Mokol\u00e9 digests faster (like a normal human)....so if you need to conserve energy....shift suchid.<br /> <br /> Reproduction: this is in the breed book and I don't have it on me RIGHT now. I can get back to your on the details but I want to say they can shift up to a certain trimester without concern. Also if you burn Rage while pregnant you have to roll stamina or miscarry. Lastly if you have your eyes on matre dice, keep in mind you only have a10% chance of 1 Mokol\u00e9 being born power clutch of eggs,not 10% per egg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 10-14-2016, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T12:48:45-07:00","id":987386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/987292-questions-about-shapechanging?p=987351#post987351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thermoregulation: I would say they switch back and forth depending on form. This is based on the merit &amp;quot;temperature control&amp;quot; from the breed book. It states with this merit a Mokol\u00e9 can with concentration control thier body temperature based on need, combinedo with the archives trait back sail (can't remember the exact name) that grants this merit in archive form. Toss in that in such I'd they are meant to be indistinguishable from a normal kin species (a 98.6 degrees croc on a 60 degree day would be distinguished). So those are my thoughts, plus the breed book does say Mokol\u00e9 need less territory due to reptiles needing less food. Lastly Mokol\u00e9 put anew emphasis on basking in the sun. They bring up how the sun is the one who warms thier bodies, they don't bask really in luna'so light. Sure they follow her, but theterrible seems a lack of emphasis on basking in moon light. Toss in the Corax only follow Helios but don't refer to him as the one who warms thier bodies....for me that's another indication of having exothermic tendencies.<br /> <br /> Metabolism: honestly when in such I'd use how long a such I'd can go without food and then be approximate for when they shift homid. So a sated croc becomes a sated homid and a hungry croc becomes a hungry homid.....also go a few months without eating only to shift homid and die seems like overkill, especially since this isn't really covered in the books. Mokol\u00e9 digestion is odd (large Archie's can eat garou, what happens when they shift?) I'd also say a homid Mokol\u00e9 digests faster (like a normal human)....so if you need to conserve energy....shift suchid.<br /> <br /> Reproduction: this is in the breed book and I don't have it on me RIGHT now. I can get back to your on the details but I want to say they can shift up to a certain trimester without concern. Also if you burn Rage while pregnant you have to roll stamina or miscarry. Lastly if you have your eyes on matre dice, keep in mind you only have a10% chance of 1 Mokol\u00e9 being born power clutch of eggs,not 10% per egg.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't really care about Matre, my character would do her duty anyway. <br /> <br /> As for eating something and then shifting, the swallow maneuver specifies that if you eat something too large and then downshift you take five levels of unsoakable damage. (Sad, cause my Archid is 24ft [7.3m] tall).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:07:43-07:00","id":987394,"title":"","content":"With the metabolic stuff, just assume that the Fera is in supernaturally good shape. So they can shrug off cold even while in Suchid, they can shrug off hunger long enough to find a cheeseburger (or shift back), etc. There's some evidence that many dinosaurs were exothermic, so I would go with exothermic with Archid form and &quot;surprisingly cool&quot; in Homid since superficial resemblances with one's Beast Form are a thing. With pregnancy there's a whole lot of precursor thinking you have to do. When Fera are knocked unconscious, they have a chance to revert to breed form. Most STs assume then that when you deliberately fall asleep, you can choose whatever form you want and stay that way. So the only limitation on what form you're in are being knocked unconscious from combat or shifting due to Frenzy. Historically, both of these things were written as being very bad for pregnancy, but more recent thinking is that Gaia isn't that dumb, that's not really how things work in the wild, and women PCs should still be able to kick ass without automatically terminating the pregnancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:52:26-07:00","id":987420,"title":"","content":"On the thermo-regulation, imo it stops when they shift out of suchid.<br /> On the eating/hunger aspect, i have always felt if you were hungry in one form, and shift, you stay hungry. If you have't eaten in one form (cause you might not need to eat as often), then your stomache will be hurting when you go homid..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}